    <name>
      <text>real-life-sequence-q1</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A learner reads a story book. The number of pages he reads each day goes up by the same amount, so the daily numbers of pages form an arithmetic progression (AP).</p>
<p>On day 1 he reads {@a@} pages, on day 4 he reads {@t4@} pages and on day 8 he reads {@t8@} pages. These forms the first three terms of a geometric progression (GP).</p>

<p>(a) Find the common difference of the AP, \(d\).</p>
<p>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>

<p>(b) Find the common ratio of the GP.</p>
<p>[[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>

<p>(c) Find the number of pages he reads on day 12.</p>
<p>[[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</p>

<p>(d) Find the total number of pages he reads in the first 8 days.</p>
<p>[[input:ans4]] [[validation:ans4]] [[feedback:prt4]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Day 1 is \( a = {@a@} \). Day 4 is {@t4@} and day 8 is {@t8@}.</p>

<p>(a) <strong>Common difference:</strong></p>
<p>Day 4 is 3 steps after day 1, so \( T_4 = a + 3d \):</p>
<p>\[ {@a@} + 3d = {@t4@} \]</p>
<p>\[ 3d = {@t4 - a@} \qquad d = {@ta1@} \]</p>
<p>Check with day 8: \( T_8 = a + 7d = {@a@} + 7 \times {@dv@} = {@t8@} \). It matches.</p>

<p>(b) <strong>Common ratio of the GP:</strong></p>
<p>\[ r = \frac{ {@t4@} }{ {@a@} } = {@ta2@} \]</p>
<p>Check: \( \frac{ {@t8@} }{ {@t4@} } = {@ta2@} \). The ratio is the same.</p>

<p>(c) <strong>Day 12:</strong></p>
<p>\[ T_{12} = a + 11d = {@a@} + 11 \times {@dv@} = {@ta3@} \text{ pages} \]</p>

<p>(d) <strong>First 8 days:</strong></p>
<p>\[ S_8 = \frac{8}{2}\left(2 \times {@a@} + 7 \times {@dv@}\right) = 4 \times {@2*a + 7*dv@} = {@ta4@} \text{ pages} \]</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
